# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch L (DeepSeek)."""
DESC_L = {
    'PT': {
        241: 'Djibril is a member of the military-industrial complex LOGOS and the new leader of Blue Cosmos, which seeks to eradicate Coordinators. He is 31 years old.\nHe is a man of excessive aristocratic tastes and biased elitist ideology. Though he normally maintains a calm and polite demeanor, when matters do not proceed as he hopes he quickly loses his temper and lashes out at objects, revealing a base character. Upon learning that the Junius Seven drop incident was the work of some Coordinators, he unilaterally declared war on PLANT on those grounds, plunging the world into chaos once again.',
        242: "Neo Roanoke is the captain of the Earth Alliance's 81st Independent Mobile Group, Phantom Pain. His rank is colonel.\nHe is a man of many mysteries, always hiding his face behind a mask and possessing an unknown history. Though he has an easygoing personality, his command and combat abilities are high, and his approachable nature and attentiveness earn him deep trust from his subordinates.\nBeyond his un-soldierly character, his high spatial awareness that allows him to freely manipulate gunbarrels, and the ability to sense the presence of Ray that occurs between them, he possesses many traits that evoke a certain person who died in the previous war.",
        243: 'This is the true form of Mu La Flaga, revealed when Neo Roanoke regained his lost memories. He is 30 years old.\nIt is believed that the recreation of the same circumstances as when he lost his memories triggered an effect similar to shock therapy. Apart from the scar on his face, he is exactly as he was before - truly a complete revival.',
        244: "Sting Oakley is an Extended belonging to the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. He stole the Chaos Gundam from ZAFT and became its pilot.\nFor Extendeds like him, a verbal safety device called a 'Block Word' is prepared to suppress their rampages. Upon hearing that word, they immediately fall into confusion and lose themselves. However, Sting's 'Block Word' has not been revealed.\nCompared to Auel and Stella, he is the most mentally stable, and he is earnest about his missions and obediently follows orders, making him the leader among the three.\nIn the battle over Berlin's city streets, he engaged the spirited Orb Murasame forces and was shot down without being able to retreat. He was believed dead, but later made a return in an unexpected form.",
        245: "Auel Neider is an Extended belonging to the Earth Alliance special forces unit Phantom Pain. He stole the Abyss Gundam from ZAFT and became its pilot.\nJust as his appearance still retains boyishness, he is capricious and free-spirited like a youth. He casually talked back to his superior Neo, ignored withdrawal orders to achieve results, and displayed numerous problems in his words and actions.\nFor Extendeds like him, a verbal safety device called a 'Block Word' is prepared to suppress their rampages. Upon hearing that word, they immediately fall into confusion and lose themselves. In Auel's case, the word is 'Mom', and he once fell into a confused state due to uttering that word himself.",
        246: "Stella Loussier was an Extended belonging to the Earth Alliance's special forces unit, Phantom Pain. She stole the Gaia Gundam from ZAFT and became its pilot.\nFor Extends such as herself, a word-based safety device called a 'block word' was prepared to suppress their rampages. Upon hearing that word, she would suddenly become confused and fall into a state of losing herself. In Stella's case, the word 'death' served this function, and she frequently fell into confusion upon hearing it.\nCompared to Sting and Auel, she was the most mentally unstable. In normal times she was timid and docile in personality, but in combat she revealed a savage destructive impulse. Whether she obeyed Neo's orders obediently in any state because of such adjustments, or because of personal feelings, remained unclear.\nReacting to Auel's words 'Mom's going to die,' she sortied alone as if to deny them. Though she was counterattacked and taken prisoner by the Minerva, she escaped danger through the hands of Shinn, who was a known acquaintance. Stella was returned on the condition that she would not be drawn into battle henceforth, but peaceful times did not visit her.",
        247: "Ian Lee was a soldier belonging to the Earth Alliance's special forces unit, Phantom Pain. His rank was Major.\nHe served as captain of the newly built ship Girty Lue, the unit's mother ship, and was a capable commander who could make calm and accurate judgments. However, after his superior Neo moved his area of operations to the ground, he was no longer seen.",
        248: "Mayu was Shinn's younger sister.\nDuring the previous war, she lived in Orb with her family, but they were exposed to the flames of war when the Earth Alliance invaded. While evacuating, she was caught in stray fire and lost her life along with her parents.\nAt that time, because Shinn had gone to retrieve the mobile phone Mayu had dropped down a slope, in the end only Shinn and Mayu's phone remained in this world.",
        249: "Sato was a deserter formerly of the ZAFT military, and the leader-like figure commanding a terrorist unit.\nTheir unit was a gathering of those who had lost loved ones in the war. For that reason, they harbored fierce anger not only toward Naturals, but also toward Coordinators who enjoyed a false peace. Believing that Patrick Zara's hardline strategy was the righteous path for revenge and reform, they plotted to drop Junius Seven onto Earth.\nA veteran soldier, his skill was genuine: while piloting the older Jin High Maneuver Type 2, he consistently overwhelmed the spec-superior GuAIZ R, and fought on at least equal footing with the new Zaku.",
        250: 'Baba was the leader of a Murasame squadron belonging to the Orb military. His rank was First Lieutenant (Captain).\nIn the battle off the coast of Crete Island, he received an order to cease fighting from Cagalli, but he continued to fight to protect his homeland.',
        251: 'President of the Atlantic Federation, one of the powerful nations belonging to the Earth Alliance. On the surface he is the supreme leader of the Earth Alliance, but in truth he is a puppet of LOGOS, and was forced by its leader, Djibril, to decide on the opening of hostilities with PLANT.',
        252: "A boy living in Urugusku who is quite ordinary except for being good at games. Seventeen years old. His parents were killed by Exodusists, so he despises the Exodus, and, carrying that emotional wound, he became a shut-in. While spending his days absorbed in the online game 'Overman Battle,' he eventually achieved 200 consecutive wins and obtained the champion title of 'King.' One day, in a prison where he was held on false charges, he met Gain and hitched onto his escape. On the way, he named the Overman he acquired 'King Gainer,' and showed off his game champion skills against the approaching Siberia Railway guard. Then, almost without meaning to, he took part in the Exodus. Because of his past experiences, he was initially quite introverted. But while various feelings - admiration for and rebellion against Gain, his feelings for Sara, and his own sense of responsibility and potential - swirled within him, he kept fighting, and became a great power in continuing the Exodus under Yapan's ceiling. At the same time, he grew as a person.",
        253: "An Exodus contractor who designs the Exodus of Urugusku. Twenty-eight years old. A master sniper whose shots from his beloved sniper rifle 'Angerma Tsaiza' never miss. He is known by the alias 'Black Southern Cross' for firing six cross-shaped bullet marks into his targets, and has a proud principle of not shooting enemies who flee with their backs turned. Because he hits on women whenever he gets the chance and says things that seem half joking and half serious, he is often thought of as a frivolous man, but in fact he has a principled and loyal character that hates dishonesty. Moreover, he is quick-witted, skilled in hand-to-hand combat, and shows excellent talent in handling silhouette machines and Overmen. In any case, he is a reliable man no matter what you ask of him, and those who know his true nature place immense trust in him. Though he does not show it, he bears many painful pasts, including tragedies experienced in his birthplace and the death of his lover. The name Gain also seems to be an alias.",
        254: 'A classmate on whom Gainer secretly harbors feelings. Seventeen years old. A cheerful and bright girl with the courage to fight in a silhouette machine as a member of the Gauli Squad, and the strength to frequently scold Gainer and Bello and to contend with Adette as a fellow woman. Her strong sense of independence seems to stem largely from the fact that she is an orphan, and perhaps for that reason she seemed to regard Gainer as a particularly pathetic man. Even so, as she acted together with him in the Exodus and their opportunities to interact increased, she eventually revised that view.',
        255: "Gainer's classmate. Twenty years old. While riding in a silhouette machine as a member of the Gauli Squad, he also serves as the helmsman of the Bachacron that tows Yapan's ceiling. Because he repeated a grade, he is older than Gainer and Sara, but despite that he is a cheerful show-off who lacks composure, and could easily pass for their age. That personality works in his favor, making him a good partner with the introverted Gainer, and they have built a friendship that could be called close friends. He has feelings for Sara and always tries to show off, but things never seem to go well.",
        256: "Gauli Hughes is the captain of the self-defense group 'Gauli Squad' in Domepolis Urgusk, aged 28. He masters a suspicious art called 'Yapan Ninpo,' and his combat abilities are extremely high, ranging from martial arts (ninjutsu) to piloting Silhouette Machines. Normally, he has a warm and personable temperament, but his true nature is that of an Exodus supremacist. He does not choose means or ends for the sake of carrying out the Exodus, and at times resorts to ruthless measures. However, Gauli himself feels conflict about his own position.",
        257: "Adette Kistler is a member of the Siberian Railway Guard, aged 25. She has a caring, big-sisterly personality, and was respected by Kejinan and Enge as 'big sis' and by Jaboli as 'older sister.' She frequently clashed with the people of Yapan's ceiling, such as fighting Gainer to stop the Exodus, infiltrating alone to seize Princess Ana, and engaging in hand-to-hand combat with Gain.",
        258: "Adette, who quit the Siberian Railway and became a teacher at the school Gainer attends. Due to the circumstances that led her there, she had no place to live and forced her way into Gainer's room as a live-in guest. Initially, she caused problems such as helping herself to the students' lunches, but with her innate adaptability, she quickly settled into Yapan's ceiling. Gainer, who lived with her, described her as 'a clumsy, rough, selfish, and truly hopeless person.' When the people of Domepolis Gangaran established a self-defense group, her combat abilities caught their eye and she was chosen as captain, forming 'Adette Squad.' She stole a Dobek from the Siberian Railway as a substitute for her severance pay and deployed it to the squad, and though her methods remained as ever, she displayed a captaincy worthy of her drive and leadership. She is only interested in strong men, and gave Gainer individual training to toughen him up. During her Siberian Railway days, her interest was in Yassaba, but now it seems to be in Gauli.",
        259: 'Ana Medal is the daughter of the Medail duke family of Domepolis Urgusk, aged 8. She was taken as a nominal hostage for carrying out the Exodus by Gain and Gainer, who accompanied him. With her abundant curiosity, she joins the Exodus while enjoying herself. She has an innocent personality befitting her age, but at times displays mature thinking and speech. When taken hostage by Asuham, she sternly condemned his actions with a composed attitude.',
        260: "Links is Ana's pet, consisting of three creatures: Link, Linna, and Lins. They look similar, but each has distinct features such as the color of their back or tail and their gaze. However, only a few people, including Ana, can tell them apart. They are extremely active, always moving around and often riding on someone's head or shoulders. Along with their owner Ana, they have become a mascot presence in Yapan's ceiling. 'Links' means 'wildcat' in English.",
        261: "Mamadou Azaf, a mechanic for the Gauli squad and a history teacher at the school attended by Gainer and the others, is 42 years old. He once served as Gainer's tutor in the past, and even now he is always finding something to nag about.",
        262: "Lyubov Smetana, a tutor and caretaker for Ana, is 20 years old. She gives an impression of being intellectual and quiet, but she does not hesitate to put herself in danger for Ana's sake. Furthermore, when Gainer appeared at the Medaille residence, she took the initiative to introduce herself, revealing that she is in fact an active and bold character.",
        263: 'Gacha Winger is one of the Five Sages of Uruksuk and their leader, at 75 years old. Since he runs a silhouette mammoth maintenance factory, he provided the silhouette mammoth for the Exodus.',
        264: 'Perha Pei is one of the Five Sages of Uruksuk, at 61 years old. She works as a doctor at a small clinic, but her hand movements are quite unsteady and her skill is not very good.',
        265: 'Sitron Bi is one of the Five Sages of Uruksuk, at 48 years old. He controls the restaurant district and himself runs numerous drinking establishments. His power seems to remain intact even after the Exodus.',
        266: 'Mannan Doutton is one of the five sages of Urgusk. He is 54 years old. He served as a close aide to Duke Medaille, but he was the one who carried out the Exodus. He has a timid and worrisome personality, and is always trembling nervously.',
        267: 'Miiya Raujin is a singer who bears the same name as the legendary first Miiya, who was once one of the five sages. She is 20 years old. She enjoys immense popularity everywhere, and she sings and dances her way toward Yapan.',
        268: "Lubu Won Dara is Miiya's manager. She is 36 years old. Though considerably older in age, she insists she is the same generation as Miiya. Having become the manager because she judged Miiya would be a source of money, she is a shrewd businesswoman who even pitches Miiya to the Siberian Railway.",
        269: "Duke Medaille is Ana's father and the lord of the domed city Urgusk. He is 51 years old. Because he collects numerous art pieces and furnishings in his castle, he is known as the 'Art Duke.' The King Gainer was one of those collectibles. He has a gentle disposition, and his governance was without issue; he was loved by his subjects as a person. When Ana first made contact after the Exodus, he showed a father's kindness by disowning her in order to avoid the danger that would threaten Ana's life, who had said she intended to return to Urgusk.",
        270: "Kona Madaya is the mechanic chief who leads the mechanics of Gauli's team. She is 27 years old. Inside the Bach Cron, which also serves as a mobile repair plant, she is in charge of maintaining machines such as the Panther and the King Gainer. She was also the one who performed the assembly work on the Emperanza. She is small-statured and baby-faced, and the word tomboy fits her perfectly; though she does not look it, she is a full decade older than Gainer and the others. She seems to have feelings for Gain, and because of that she is often talked around by him.",
        271: "Yassaba Jin was the captain of the Siberian Railway Guard. He was 32 years old.\nHe devoted himself wholeheartedly to stopping the Exodus and rooting out Exodus sympathizers, and he would stop at nothing to accomplish those goals. Yet his character was more that of a warrior than a soldier; he showed a willingness to admit defeat with grace, and occasionally revealed a gentleness toward those without power.\nHe persistently attacked the 'Yapan Ceiling,' but each time he was thwarted by King Gainer, suffering defeat after defeat. Though he was once taken prisoner, he escaped by seizing an opportunity, and during his flight he encountered the fortune-telling girl Eifa. He rescued the girl, who had been mistreated by her boss, but in the ensuing battle he was defeated once again.\nWith his options exhausted, Yassaba carried out the Exodus together with Eifa. But during their escape they encountered a Golem, and he was struck by gunfire, after which his fate became unknown.",
        272: 'Kejinan Dadd was a member of the Siberian Railway Guard. He was 31 years old.\nHe had a simple, easy-to-read personality: he fawned over the strong and was overbearing toward the weak.\nWhen his captain Yassaba lost his Overman, he tried to have him killed and take over as captain himself, and when he found himself in a position superior to Adette, he took advantage of it to press a marriage proposal. Regardless of who he was dealing with, his actions remained consistent. In a sense, one could say he was a man of unwavering character to the core.',
        273: 'Enge Gam was a member of the Siberian Railway Guard. He was 30 years old.\nWith his stern face and eyepatch, he gave the impression of a tough, rugged man, but inwardly he had a somewhat pessimistic disposition.\nHe subscribed to the idea of being number two rather than number one, and always yielded the initiative to Kejinan, with whom he always acted in concert. However, this was largely a means of avoiding responsibility when trouble arose. And beneath it all, he harbored a dark cunning, ready to discard Kejinan at any moment if the need arose.',
        274: "Jaboli Mariera was a member of the Siberian Railway Guard. He was 23 years old.\nHe was born and raised in the countryside and carried a deep inferiority complex about it. He felt a strong admiration for Saint Reigan of London IMA, which seemed to embody the city, and especially for Asuham, whom he adored and addressed as 'Lady White Lily.' Asuham called him the 'Man of the Wild Rose,' but in truth it seemed he was regarded as little more than a convenient pawn.\nHe handled Silhouette Machines and Overmen competently, but since he had never shot anyone, he was poor at using firearms, revealing a side of him unaccustomed to violence.",
        275: "Kashmar Bare was the operations director of the Siberian Railway. He was 39 years old.\nHe hated nothing more than having the railway timetable disrupted, and his ruthlessness in maintaining the schedule at any cost earned him the nickname 'the Ice Operations Director.'\nHe was dispatched as captain of the Railway Guard to fill the gap left by the vanished Yassaba, and above all to stop the Exodus of the 'Yapan Ceiling,' the very source of the timetable disruptions.\nHe spoke in a feminine manner, wore purple lipstick and a mohawk, and favored psycho Overmen that sowed unease or read minds. Both in appearance and in substance, he was a thoroughly unmanly figure.\nAside from timetable disruptions, what he hated most was healthy relationships between men and women, and that had once proven to be his undoing.",
        276: "Asuham Boone is the captain of the special forces unit 'Saint Reigan' of the London IMA police organization that governs Domepolis. His rank is special lieutenant, and he is 28 years old. He is an elite with handsome looks and high practical ability, expected to have a bright future. His refined demeanor strongly attracted Jaboli. However, he actually has a sociable but easily excitable personality, and to achieve his goals he will calmly resort to treachery and taking hostages. He is not merely a handsome face but, in a sense, a man full of human warmth. He ostensibly uses the prevention of the Exodus as his reason, but more than that, he devotes himself to capturing Gainer, repeatedly launching attacks on the ceiling of Yapan. The reason was that Gainer had previously laid hands on Asuham's sister Karin and then left her, so Asuham was trying to bring him back. Later, in order to corner Gainer, he voluntarily removed himself from the elite course and transferred to the Siberian Railway Guard.",
        277: "Zacky Bronco is the deputy captain of the Asuham Boone special forces unit of Saint Reigan. He is 24 years old. He possesses ability befitting his position, and expertly pilots Golem-type Overmen. He obediently follows Asuham's orders, but behind the scenes there was a side of him that quietly mocked Asuham, who pursued Gainer with blatant personal motives. When heading for the castle of Kids Munto, he was attacked and shot down by Cynthia's Dominator, and sank to the bottom of Lake Baikal.",
        278: "Karin Boone is Asuham's beloved younger sister. Gainer had previously laid hands on her, and a child was conceived at that time. When she eventually gave birth to a girl, Asuham found himself fighting desperately to bring Gainer back.",
        279: "Kids Munto is the president of the Siberian Railway Corporation. He is 61 years old. Using the Crystal of Agat as his stronghold, he schemes to collect the parts of the Overdevil that the first Miya sealed away and make its power his own. He is called the 'Railroad King' and, while already possessing ample status and power, is an ambitious man who seeks even greater strength, though he sometimes shows oddly childish behavior. It is hard to imagine from his appearance, which has been described as a 'wicked Buddha statue', but he is so accustomed to fighting that he can defeat an armed Asuham in a counterattack.",
        280: "Martina Lane is Cynthia's grandmother. She is the bearer of the powerful Oversense that was passed down to her granddaughter. She has personally experienced the Over Freeze, and knows the terror of the Overdevil better than anyone.",
        281: "Cynthia Lane is the prized protege of Kids Munto, eighteen years old. She is a girl who always has confectionery in her mouth, with a guileless personality and small stature, leaving much childishness about her. However, her mother and grandmother come from a bloodline with powerful Oversense, and having been raised with elite training as an Overman pilot, she possesses combat ability beyond what her appearance would suggest. She has been acquainted with Gainer through games for some time, being both rival and friend, and holds the title of 'Queen,' the female counterpart to Gainer's title of 'King.' There is a tendency in her to view combat aboard an Overman as an extension of gaming.",
        282: 'Eifa is a girl who runs a fortune-telling stall in Urgusk. She meets the fugitive Yassaba and becomes close to him after sheltering him. Having been mistreated by her master, she is invited by Yassaba to join the Exodus toward the Indus region, but she vanishes in a blast of wind after being shot at by a Golem attempting to stop them.',
        283: "Roger Smith is the foremost negotiator in Paradigm City, a town that has lost its memories, aged twenty-five. He advances negotiations with a humorous and witty tone, delivering results beyond what his clients expect. He is fundamentally a feminist and a gentleman, but he is quick to lose his temper, and against those who refuse to listen to his words and break good faith and rules, he may resort to force. However, he makes it a principle never to carry a gun, no matter how dangerous the job. He has a past as a former military police lieutenant, and is an old acquaintance of Dastun. He is a stubborn man who dislikes bending his own views, but when Dorothy says she wants to keep a cat, he ends up granting such earnest wishes despite his grumbling, showing a good-natured side. He holds the memory of piloting Big O, and with Big O confronts great evils. This is by no means an act of playing at being a hero, but the result of straightforward anger toward those who break good faith and human rules. Roger himself does not know why he holds the memory to pilot Big O. He makes his home in a ruined bank on 72nd Street, Out of the Dome. Because Roger has an extreme preference for black, everyone living in his mansion is required to wear black clothing. Also, only women may enter his mansion unconditionally. His hobby is collecting hourglasses, and he also makes them himself. He places great importance on a refreshing awakening, though his poor rising from sleep has seen him roused by Dorothy's extreme piano playing.",
        284: "R. Dorothy Wayneright is an android created by Timothy Wayneright in the likeness of his own daughter. However, she is quite heavy, weighing 130 kilograms. Lacking the funds to pay her reward for the affair concerning Wayneright's inheritance, she chose to work as a maid in Roger's mansion. Not only is she highly complete as an android, but she displays rich expressions to Wayneright, showers affection on cats, and poses questions about love to Roger, being made as a being very close to human. Thus, Roger is sometimes seen forgetting that she is an android. The 'R' stands for the R in 'Robot.' Her unfriendly and high-handed attitude sometimes leaves Roger at a loss, but over time she became his good partner. The headband portion of her head is a memory drive, often used as a light source as well. Playing the piano is her hobby, but her initial repertoire consisted only of violent musical pieces. However, under the instruction of the pianist android R. Instole, the breadth of her playing gradually expanded.",
        285: "Norman Berg is a butler serving Roger, aged fifty-four. Long before Roger came to the ruined bank, he followed the memory of Big O's maintenance and awaited the arrival of his master. He ably handles not only Big O's upkeep but also the maintenance of Roger's beloved car 'Griffon' and all household affairs of the mansion, displaying his versatile abilities daily for Roger's sake. Given his performance, it is no exaggeration to say that Roger's private life is sustained thanks to him. He possesses an iron spirit unshaken by anything, and even when Roger was kidnapped, he worried but remained calm and composed without panicking. He also showed a powerful side, racing through battle zones on a large motorcycle with sidecar, and wielding heavy firearms when enemies attacked.",
        286: "Duston is the chief of the Paradigm military police and commander of the mobile unit, aged 47. He takes pride in his work with the military police and is a rugged man who faithfully follows his duties. He is also a man of justice who will defy orders from above and act on his own judgment to protect citizens, both inside and outside the dome. Many subordinates admire him and act alongside him. With Roger, his former subordinate, he sometimes clashes, but at the bottom of their hearts they trust each other and have built a good friendship. During the Megadeus incident, he grew frustrated with his own powerlessness and that of the military police, and began to doubt the very worth of the military police's existence.",
        287: "Angel is a woman of unknown identity, with almost everything about her, including her nationality and age, shrouded in mystery. She calls herself Angel because of scars on her back that look as though wings once grew there. Her motives are unclear, but she appears before Roger at every opportunity, seemingly aiming to obtain memory data. She possesses a strong personality that does not flinch before anyone, and the drive to go even to the dangerous bottom of the sea if it means getting the memory. She is registered with Paradigm Corporation, but her actions do not seem to prioritize the company's interests.",
        288: "Beck is a criminal who commits misdeeds in Paradigm City, aged 22. He appears with vulgar laughter and engages in all manner of crimes, including bank robbery, kidnapping, and fraud. His speech and conduct are those of a petty thug, and Roger calls him 'a criminal unworthy of the title professional.' Because he holds memory data on alternative interface technology essential for operating Megadeus, he procures Megadeus units and uses them in his crimes. After being sent to prison by Roger in the Soldano heiress kidnapping incident, he calls Roger 'that crow bastard' and swears revenge. He repeatedly escapes prison and devises schemes time and again to send Roger to his doom.",
        289: "T-Bone is Beck's subordinate. Together with Dove, he helped Beck escape from prison.",
        290: "Dove is Beck's pale-skinned subordinate. He is characterized by speaking in an effeminate manner.",
        291: "A memory digger who investigates the truth behind memories lost over 40 years ago. Once a newspaper reporter for Paradigm Press under the name Michael Seebach, he became obsessed with pursuing the truth and eventually discovered the Archetype at the bottom of an underground corridor. However, when he unlocked it, his entire body was left wrapped in bandages. Incidentally, Schwarzvalt means 'black forest' in German. Later, he discovered the Big Duo and challenged Roger to a duel but was defeated. At that time, he was shocked to see the Big Duo act on its own and vanished from the public stage. He has a habit of speaking with meaningful words, as if reciting poetry. He looks down on those who do not seek the truth and merely live in the present.",
        292: 'The head of Paradigm Corporation, which rules Paradigm City. Aged 43. Born as the legitimate child of Gordon, who built up the Paradigm Group, he is a man full of a sense of omnipotence who boasts that he was chosen to be the ruler. Because of this, he has a mentally childish side, and his self-centered words and actions stand out. He also holds strong elitist beliefs and thoroughly looks down on the residents living outside the dome.',
        293: "A masked man who serves Alex and works in the shadows. As a 'Boogie' with half his body mechanized, he possesses tremendous physical abilities and considers himself 'a being beyond human'. He has an abnormal disposition, cold-blooded and sadistic, taking pleasure in killing. When he confronted Dorothy in a ruined church, he sent footage of a wounded Dorothy to the Big O's monitor, attempting to show Roger his atrocity.",
        294: "The first head of the Paradigm Group. He has now left the company to his legitimate child Alex and devotes himself to cultivating artificial tomatoes at a farm on the outskirts. His immense influence remains intact to this day. He is a person who may know the truth of the memories, and when Roger visited him, he cast words suggesting that something had occurred between himself and Roger. In his unfinished book 'Metropolis', he recorded events believed to have taken place 40 years ago.",
        295: "A killer clad in a red raincoat. He awakened from a container left underground in a marshalling yard and, using a handgun, murdered one after another those who had recalled memories from over 40 years ago. His motive was an order he heard from the moment of awakening. The face beneath the hood was that of an android closely resembling Dorothy. The 'R' stands for 'RED', and the 'D' stands for 'DESTINY'.",
        296: "Vera Ronstadt is a member of the foreign organization Union and its de facto leader. Her code name is Number 12. She appeared in Paradigm City to take responsibility for her subordinates' repeated failures. As the one who held the Union members together, she was considered to have considerable power within the organization. However, after failing to punish Alex for betraying the Union and having many of her comrades captured, she rapidly began to lose that power.",
        297: 'Big Ear is an information broker and an acquaintance of Roger. He is 49 years old. He is well-versed in all kinds of information, both within Paradigm City and beyond. He always sits in the same seat at the seedy bar Speakeasy, reading the newspaper while waiting for customers.',
        298: 'Touga Tenkuuji is the pilot of God Gravion and its core unit, Gran Kaiser. He is 17 years old. During his early childhood in an orphanage, his strong G Factor was recognized, and he was adopted by Sandman. Since then, he has undergone combat training at St. Germain Castle to become the Gran Kaiser pilot. As a result, his personality has become quite detached from the real world. Normally gentle and personable, once he enters battle he coldly destroys enemies like a combat machine. In that state, he prioritizes defeating the enemy above all else and does not balk at accepting some casualties. This imbalance sometimes leads him to hurt others without realizing it. However, through his interactions with Eiji, who is his complete opposite, he comes to recognize what he lacks and begins to suffer over it.',
        299: "Eiji Shigure is the pilot of G Attacker, which forms the right leg of God Gravion. He is 17 years old. His surname is read 'Shigure'. He has an intense sister complex, valuing Ayaka, the sister who raised him since childhood, above all else. When she went missing, he infiltrated St. Germain Castle alone to search for her. By chance, he boarded the G Attacker, and that became the catalyst for him becoming a pilot. His personality is hot-blooded, and he is a constant troublemaker, with ignoring orders and going out without permission being routine. To Touga, he is truly a bad influence, filling the naive boy's head with all sorts of knowledge and dragging him into reckless situations. On the other hand, Eiji has also boarded the Gran Kaiser out of rivalry with Touga. However, he frequently clashed with Touga, angered by his willingness to accept sacrifices in battle and his attitude of disregarding others' feelings.",
        300: "Runa Gusuku is the pilot of G Driller, which forms the left arm of God Gravion. She is 16 years old. Her surname is read 'Gusuku'. She is a lively girl from Okinawa who wears her emotions on her sleeve, giving her a very expressive face. She possesses the bravery to face harsh battles without fear. Since meeting Touga at St. Germain Castle as a child, when her father brought her there, she has harbored a budding romantic feelings for him. As a result, she is jealous of Eiji, who appeared later and grew close to Touga despite being another boy. This is one reason the two are constantly fighting, but through their repeated squabbling, it seems she has also begun to take some interest in Eiji. She deeply respects her late father, and she joined the Grand Knights to carry on his will, which he had reported the discovery of Zeravire at the cost of his life.",
        301: 'A pilot of the G Striker, which forms the left leg of God Gravion. She is 22 years old.\nA professional fighter who received her training at Saint Germain Castle. She provides the mental support that keeps the Gran Knights, many of whose members are still inexperienced, on an even keel.\nShe has a hobby of seducing men, and during a hot springs trip she reverse-picked up Alex. Yet at the same time, she has no interest in men who fall for her - a complex personality, to say the least.\nShe is a close friend of Ayaka, and she cooperated with Eiji in his search for Ayaka, who is believed to be somewhere within Saint Germain Castle.',
        302: 'A pilot of the G Driller, which forms the right arm of God Gravion. She is 16 years old. Normally she works as a maid at Saint Germain Castle.\nShe is serious and earnest in everything she does, and she always strives to be of use to someone, but her natural clumsiness often ends up causing trouble for those around her instead. Still, because she has been looking after Touga since he was small, she is like a mother to him.\nAlthough she is timid and lacks confidence in herself, she harbors a strong will beneath the surface, one that would not hesitate to risk her life for the sake of her comrades.',
        303: "A pilot of the Geo Javelin, which forms the right arm of Sol Gravion.\nShe is an artificial life form called the 'Proto Grandiva' created by Sandman, and she is also the original Eina's true body.\nBecause she inherited Eina's memory data as-is, her personality has not changed at all. However, her appearance has undergone a major image change: the color of her hair, the design of her maid uniform and battle suit, and a lower rate of wearing glasses, among other things.",
        304: 'A pilot of the G Shadow, which forms the head and chest of God Gravion. She is 14 years old. She spends all her time, except when sortieing, with her pet and best friend, a ferret named Rolot.\nShe was found collapsed and suffering from memory loss, and was taken in by Sandman. Since then, she lived in the south tower of Saint Germain Castle without ever coming into contact with anyone other than Sandman. As a result, she initially kept her heart closed to others, but through repeated battles and daily life as a member of the Gran Knights, a sense of camaraderie gradually sprouted within her, and she came to show a variety of expressions.',
        305: "The lord of Saint Germain Castle and one of the world's wealthiest men. Using his knowledge and financial resources, he organized Asgard and protects the peace of Earth as its supreme commander. However, his past and true identity are shrouded in mystery.\nHe possesses his own unique aesthetic, and is a flawless individual who carries out anything he does in a stylish manner. He has many fans even among the maids working at Saint Germain Castle.",
        306: "Sandman is a false name; his real name is 'Zig Ehrlichmeyer'. A scientist from the planet Lambias, he developed the Genesis machine 'Gran Sigma', capable of destroying or even creating planets, in order to save his dying homeworld. However, a difference of opinion brought him into conflict with his brother-in-law Hyugi, and as a result, Lambias collapsed. He escaped Lambias in the 'Gran Sigma' and eventually reached Earth. Over the long years that followed, he built the Proto Grandiva, God Gravion, and other machines to protect Earth from his brother-in-law, who would one day come seeking revenge. By using the G Factor within his body as a metabolic function, his hair turned purple, and he became immortal and ageless. However, because he boarded the 'Gran Sigma' and released his G Factor in order to fight, he has reverted to his original blond hair.",
        307: "The combat commander of Asgard. He always conceals his face behind a mask, which cannot be removed without Sandman's permission. He possesses an unyielding will, always maintaining the composure to correctly assess any situation. In an emergency, he issues precise orders to the Gran Knights and the combat maid unit. He enjoys Sandman's deep trust and becomes the highest authority during Sandman's absence. Because of this position, he is often left behind to mind the fort when the others go on vacations or to hot springs, a fact that deeply grieves him. He is also in charge of training the Gran Knights, and he is particularly hard on Eiji. When the Zeravire began their full-scale invasion, he removed his mask in order to spur on Sandman, who was cowering in fear of Hyugi's shadow, using his own voice and words.",
        308: "Eiji's older sister. A former member of the EFA, she fell in love with Sandman while infiltrating Saint-Germain Castle on reconnaissance. Though she possesses the G Factor, its power was too weak for her to pilot Grandiva. To support him, she chose to conceal her identity and succeed the mantle of 'Raven', without even telling the truth to her close friend Mizuki. In her role as 'Raven', when conducting Gran Knight training or punishment, she was especially strict with Eiji. Whether this stemmed from sisterly affection or was a penalty for his insolent talk toward Sandman remains a fine line. When Sandman lost his will to fight, cowering in fear of Hyugi's shadow, she removed the Raven mask and rallied him with her own words.",
        309: 'One of the three operator maids who support the Gran Knights during battle. Always striving for perfection, she is a reliable sort and serves as the leader of the trio. Her excessive seriousness gives her a habit of endlessly brooding over problems. Moreover, she drives herself into a spiral of further anguish, worrying that her earnest demeanor might be creating an unapproachable atmosphere around her beloved Sandman.',
        310: "One of the three operator maids who support the Gran Knights during battle. Her catchphrase is 'payok'. She is fickle and easily carried away, and is often scolded by Tesera. Even so, her natural cheerfulness, which spreads energy to those around her, is her charm.",
        311: 'One of the three operator maids who support the Gran Knights during battle.\nShe is a modest and considerate person, and her gentle manner makes her look the most mature of the three. However, she is very interested in romance talk and will always stick her nose into it whenever she gets the chance.',
        312: 'One of the three little maids, and their leader figure.\nWhile claiming to look after Eiji, she takes off his clothes and charges into his bath.\nShe is always energetic, cheerful, and mischievous, with a hobby of games in general. She never loses at gambling games with Eiji, and once made the Gran Knights serve as maids for a day as payment for her winnings.',
        313: 'One of the three little maids.\nWhile claiming to look after Eiji, she takes off his clothes and charges into his bath.\nShe is naturally honest and gentle, but because she is always acting together with Brigitta, she tends to be thought of as being on the same level of brattiness.',
        314: 'One of the three little maids.\nShe has taken a liking to Eiji, and while claiming to look after him, she takes off his clothes and charges into his bath.\nShe is shy and quiet, but she also possesses boldness that surprises those around her, such as when she went alone to rescue Rozlot while he was in the middle of a Zeravire attack.',
        315: 'An SP maid who protects the safety of all those involved with Saint-Germain Castle, and the leader of the combat unit.\nShe excels at command, fully controlling and leading the combat unit. Her individual combat ability is also immense, and the power unleashed by her trained body far surpasses that of Eiji.\nHer work is wide-ranging: she serves as bodyguard when Sandman leaves the castle, searches for the Gran Knights when they go missing, and even serves as main pilot of the Gran Fortress, the transport plane for God Gravion.',
        316: "Toria is a mechanic maid who handles maintenance of all machinery, including the Gran Kaiser, and serves as the head of the maintenance crew. She pours limitless affection into machines, and for the sake of tinkering with them she can easily go without sleep or meals. She completed the 'Phantom System' that remotely pilots the Grandiva in an extremely short time, and her excellence as a mechanic is remarkable. However, it cannot be denied that she is somewhat prone to running wild, such as independently developing new armament for the God Gravion without even telling Sandman. When the Grand Fortress launches, she rides aboard as a sub-pilot.",
        317: "Faye Xinlu is the captain of the G Soldier unit belonging to the Earth Federation government EFA, with the rank of First Lieutenant. Written in kanji, her name is 'Fei Xin Lu.' During combat in the Gran Trooper, she issues formation orders to each unit. Her piloting skill is of course superb, and she possesses excellent athletic ability and a sharp intellect, earning deep trust from both subordinates and superiors. She spent her early childhood in the same orphanage as Touga, but the fact that Sandman chose Touga over her became a complex, and she resolved to always be superior to Touga. That feeling became a burden, and at times it caused her to misjudge when to withdraw in battle. She often scolded her subordinate Alex for his seemingly frivolous attitude, but their relationship was never actually a bad one.",
        318: "Alex Smith is a member of the G Soldier unit belonging to the Earth Federation government EFA, with the rank of Lieutenant. He was originally in the air force, serving as a fighter pilot. However, he was injured in an attack by a Zeravire during a mission, and after recovering he was transferred into the G Soldier unit. From then on, he rode in a Gran Trooper whose main armament was a gun. He is fundamentally lighthearted in personality, and his favorite things are girls, robots, and Japan. Faye reprimanded him many times for his overly enthusiastic remarks and behavior. However, he also encouraged Faye when she was troubled, and even in desperate situations he endured while believing in the Gravion's arrival, showing that he has a passionate side beneath his joker exterior.",
        319: "Hans is a member of the G Soldier unit belonging to the Earth Federation government EFA. He is from Germany. His marksmanship is the best in the unit, and he possesses the skill to always hit exactly where he aims. The machine he pilots is also focused on shooting, and he can attack numerous Zeravires simultaneously. However, contrary to his ability, he has a boyish innocence - delighting in the Gran Trooper's performance and enjoying battles against the Zeravires like a game.",
        320: "Iwan is a member of the G Soldier unit belonging to the Earth Federation government EFA. He is from Russia. He suppresses his emotions and analyzes enemy forces with ice-cold, piercing eyes, serving as the unit's strategic advisor. However, he is also something of a narcissist who occasionally becomes passionately enamored with himself. In his Gran Trooper, during 'Attack Formation V,' he serves as the connector to Faye's machine.",
        321: 'Jose is a member of the G Soldier team belonging to the Earth Federation Government EFA. He is from Brazil.\nWith his cheerful and friendly personality, he quickly blends in with the children. He is skilled at soccer, and even the weapon of his Gran Trooper is a soccer ball, showing his particular attachment.\nHe always displays effeminate gestures, and seems to be making advances toward Ian whenever he gets the chance.',
        322: 'William Wallace Fitzgerald is the highest authority of the Earth Federation Government EFA (EFA), serving as President.\nHe was capable and frank in personality, handling government affairs without trouble, but was hard-pressed by the sudden appearance of Zeravire. His insistence on preserving his dignity as the supreme leader led him to take an uncooperative attitude toward Sandman, who wielded the power of Gravion.\nHe had the Gran Troopers developed so that the EFA alone could repel the Zeravire.',
        323: "Hugi Zeravire is the elder brother of Sandman's wife Lufira, and the leader of the Zeravire.\nOriginally an excellent scientist, he developed the mass slaughter system 'Genocideron' to save the inhabitants of his dying home planet Lambia from environmental deterioration, by exterminating the people of planet Celia and securing a place to emigrate. However, he clashed with Sandman, who advocated environmental restoration through the Genesis machine 'Gran Sigma', and in an accident during that confrontation, he was trapped within the runaway 'Genocideron'.\nAfter being absorbed into the system, his desire for revenge against Sandman was amplified, and his mental balance was lost. Combined with his belief that Sandman was responsible for the death of his beloved sister Lufira, he came to resolve to attack Earth with the destruction machines 'Zeravire' that the system had created.",
        324: "Lufira is Hugi's younger sister. She was wed to Sandman and bore him a beloved daughter, Leele.\nShe had always been frail, and could not endure the strain of childbirth, passing away in exchange for Leele's birth. However, she was revived as an artificial life-form by Hugi, who could not accept her death.\nShe has no soul dwelling within her, and has become a puppet obedient to Hugi's commands.",
        325: "Lorrot is a ferret who is Leele's pet and also her best friend.\nShe spends all her time with Leele except when Leele sorties.",
        326: "A boy regarded as the reincarnation of 'Wing of the Sun' Apollonius. Estimated age 13.\nHaving been orphaned during the great catastrophe 11 years ago, he joined forces with Baron and others in the same situation and lived tough as a street child.\nIn addition to a rare wild intuition, he has amazing eyesight of 5.0 or better in both eyes, and a keen sense of smell that can distinguish even the scent of infrared rays, let alone body odor, making him worthy of being called a wild child.\nHis personality is straightforward for better or worse, and he tends to act in ways that could be seen as selfish. Though he seems to lack any sense of solidarity, he harbors a passionate friendship that fears no danger for the sake of his comrades. He boarded Aquarion in order to rescue Baron, who had been captured by the Shadow Angels.\nFor a while after entering the Element School, he frequently caused trouble due to unfamiliar group life and standard play. However, through battle he acquired cooperation and teamwork, and along with that, he began to remember his past life.",
        327: "A first-class Element attending the Element School. Age 14.\nShe is a princess of the old Kingdom of Alicia, carrying the bloodline of Apollonius and Celian. She has the ability to emit psychokinesis by gathering ki in her left arm, allowing her to lift or bend any object.\nPerhaps because she lost her parents at a young age, she harbors an abnormal affection for her older brother Sirius. As a result, she is wary of all women who approach Sirius, and especially harbors hostility toward Reika. She inherits the past life of Celian, and was convinced that the reincarnation of her former lover 'Wing of the Sun' was Sirius. However, when faced with the fact that the wild child Apollo, who suddenly appeared one day, might actually be the 'Wing of the Sun,' she stubbornly refused to accept it. But with the help of her own past life memories, she gradually came to acknowledge it.",
        328: "A first-class Element attending the Element School. Age 16.\nHe is the prince of the old Kingdom of Alicia and Silvia's older brother. He cherishes a rose named Alicia, recites poetry at every opportunity, and pours his affection on all beautiful things. He recognizes Reika's bearing as beautiful and holds feelings for her. However, since he thoroughly rejects ugliness and savagery, which are the opposite, he constantly clashes with Apollo, who is a mass of wildness. Regarding Apollo specifically, his frustration at being unable to recall his own past life and jealousy toward him are also largely involved.\nHe possesses the Element ability to emit high-speed vibrations from his right arm, and by transmitting this to a sword, he can produce astonishing cutting power. His hearing also far exceeds that of ordinary people.",
        329: "A first-class Element attending the Element School. Age 15. Her name is read as 'Kou Reika.'\nHer Element abilities are strong spiritual sensitivity and psychometry that reads records. However, because her abilities are too powerful, she attracts trouble wherever she goes. She is a 'woman who calls misfortune' acknowledged by both herself and others.\nFearing that she might involve those who approach her, she tends to show a demeanor that keeps others at a distance and a dark, downcast expression. But in truth she has a rich sensitivity, and her specialty is sports in general, making her active.\nShe believed that Glen's serious injury on her first sortie was due to the misfortune she spreads, and feared combining, sinking even deeper into gloom. However, through Commander Fudo's training and surviving battles, she gradually overcame her negative emotions.",
        330: 'A first-class Element attending the Element School. Age 17.\nHe has the Element ability to control fire, and is a hot-blooded man burning in both body and spirit. He was once active as a professional soccer player, but joined DEAVA after all his teammates and spectators were taken by a Mythical Beast during a match.\nPerhaps considering himself the mood maker of the Elements, he always brightens the atmosphere with his innate cheerfulness. However, when Apollo went out of control thinking only of himself, he showed a sportsmanlike side that values harmony, shouting at him to cooperate and face the enemy.\nHe is thought to be a frivolous man who hits on any woman he sees, but this behavior comes from his own bravado to cover up the heartbreak of his first love, Esperansa, having married his older brother Lopes.',
        331: "Jun is a first-class Element attending the Element School. He is 14 years old. He is strong with machines and computers, and his true value shines in intellectual work such as information analysis. His knowledge of hacking in particular runs deep, and he can access state secrets at will. On the other hand, his lack of physical strength is conspicuous, and he always struggles with the training that Commander Fudo assigns. He is also an idol otaku, and his favorite figure 'Manamana-chan' is displayed on top of the computer in his room. As an Element, he possesses the ability of thoughtography, projecting images onto film or digital screens. However, he cannot see the images directly until they are actually projected. He has feelings for Tsugumi, who entered the Element School at the same time as him, but Tsugumi's heart seems to be elsewhere, and their relationship never seems to progress.",
        332: 'Tsugumi is a first-class Element attending the Element School. She is 15 years old. She is a bright and cheerful girl, but she sometimes makes major blunders. Though one would not imagine it from her usual timid demeanor, she also harbors an earnest, headstrong passionate side. She also seems to hold feelings for her senior Reika that go beyond mere respect and admiration. Her hobby and specialty is tinkering with machinery, and her skill is such that she once repaired her beloved car, the Isetta, which she received from her grandfather. Her Element ability causes explosions around her when her excitement reaches its peak. Because of this, she was ostracized by others in her childhood, and it remains a trauma to this day.',
        333: "Reena is a mysterious girl of unknown age who serves as an Element belonging to DEAVA. She possesses very strong psychic sensitivity, and has the Element ability to judge people's hearts and the surrounding environment through the shape and color of their auras. She is also a prophet who performs various divinations using the 'Book of Genesis,' and her abilities are highly regarded within DEAVA. She absorbs prana from blood and can teleport without using the Element Change System, among other mysteries, to the point that rumors of her being a vampire once circulated. However, with Apollo's help, her comrades eventually came to recognize that her special powers, too, were simply part of who Reena is.",
        334: 'Glen was a first-class Element at the Element School who posted results on par with Sirius and Reika. He was 17 years old. In addition to his kindhearted personality, he possessed superior qualities as an Element. He had built a firm relationship of trust with Sirius and the others. In his first actual combat, he achieved union with Reika, for whom he harbored feelings. However, he was hit during that battle and suffered severe injuries.',
        335: "Glen, revived from a coma after having the wings of Fubaki transplanted into him. The gentleness he once showed is gone, and he has become an expressionless, cold-blooded combat machine. He stood in the way of the Cherudim Mars piloted by Sirius with an Assault-type Aquarion, when Sirius attempted to break through DEAVA's barrier.",
        336: 'Chloe Kurik is a first-class Element attending the Element School. She is 14 years old. Aside from their clothing, she and her fraternal twin brother Kurt share almost no physical differences. She possesses the Element ability of telepathy, which manifests most powerfully between herself and Kurt. She sometimes sortied aboard a Vector Machine, but as her support abilities were apparently stronger, she primarily participated in battle as an operator.',
        337: 'Kurt Kurik is a first-class Element attending the Element School. He is 14 years old. Aside from their clothing, he and his fraternal twin sister Chloe share almost no physical differences. He possesses the Element ability of telepathy, which manifests most powerfully between himself and Chloe. He sometimes sortied aboard a Vector Machine, but as his support abilities were apparently stronger, he primarily participated in battle as an operator.',
        338: "Fudo GEN is the commander of the Aquarion deployment unit of the special agency 'DEAVA, the Earth Regeneration Organization.' He also serves as an instructor at the Element School. His age is unknown. He appears and disappears at will, showing up anywhere, earning him the nickname 'the Magician of Divine Speed.' He has mastered a wide and deep range of skills, from magic tricks such as producing arrows from nowhere or suddenly enlarging sheets of paper, to astonishing abilities like reading people's minds, summoning wild hawks with a single finger, and discerning a person's personality and preferences from their footprints alone. Aside from having been a member of the Aquarion excavation survey team, his past history is entirely unknown. Even how he became commander is a mystery, yet his words carry a strange persuasiveness. He constantly gives the Elements hints to overcome difficulties, guiding them to victory.",
        339: "Jean Jerome Georges is the vice commander of DEAVA's Aquarion deployment unit. He is 24 years old. He has been involved in the organization's founding since he was a boy, and several members of his family hold positions in DEAVA's upper ranks. He possesses a genius intellect, holding doctorates in various fields such as military and defense science, and has mastered thirteen languages. However, his overly serious personality works against him, leaving him inflexible and unable to conduct operations with adaptability, which is his drawback. As a result, in the presence of Commander Fudo, who leads the Elements with bold actions and weighty words, he tends to be overshadowed. In addition, the unruly behavior of the overly individualistic Elements is a constant source of headaches for him.",
        340: 'Sophia Blanc is a psychotherapist responsible for the mental care of the Elements and candidates at the Element School. She is 27 years old. Although she is not an Element ability user herself, she possesses abundant knowledge and experience regarding the worries and doubts unique to ability users. Furthermore, as she is a leading researcher in the study of combination, she serves as a great pillar of support for the boys and girls on the psychological front.',
        341: "Baron was Apollo's close friend and the leader of the street children. When Apollo first met Baron, he had no name, but Baron, seeing him as if he had appeared from the rising morning sun, gave him the name 'Apollo'. He was carried off by a harvesting beast along with the other companions right before Apollo's eyes.",
        342: "Zushi, also known as Thoma, was a holy Shadow Angel of the Shadow Angel tribe and the front-line commander who led the other Shadow Angels. He had wings on the back of his head, but aside from that, his appearance was the closest to human among the Shadow Angels. Twelve thousand years ago, he was betrothed to Apollonius, the strongest guardian Shadow Angel. However, when Apollonius betrayed the Shadow Angels at the end of the Atlantia War, Zushi faced him as an enemy. Yet his love had not faded even now, and he repeatedly made contact with Apollo, who seemed to be Apollonius's reincarnation. Incidentally, 'Shadow Angel' was a derogatory term used by humans for the Shadow Angels, who called themselves 'Winged Ones' - the derogatory term humans used among the Shadow Angels was 'wingless ones' or 'wingless people'. However, it could be said that only Apollonius, who betrayed the Shadow Angel tribe, was truly a 'Shadow Angel' in their eyes.",
        343: "Otoha was the music wing of the Shadow Angel tribe. At first glance she appeared as a beautiful woman, but beneath her robes she concealed a snake-like lower half. The parts that looked like eyebrows were also eyes, and when her emotions ran high, all four eyes would open wide. As the lover of the holy Shadow Angel Zushi in the present age, she burned with dark jealousy toward Apollonius, who still attracted Zushi's heart. The wings covering both her arms could be strummed like a harp or produce fine vibrations to make music. Though the tone was beautiful, it held powerful demonic qualities that could drive listeners mad or even manipulate the weather.",
        344: "Yohanes was an aged wise wing who governed the darkness of the world. He was an elder of the Shadow Angel tribe and one of the development members who had performed genetic manipulation on the 'wings' born from sudden mutation, evolving them into 'Shadow Angels'. Much of his body had already been lost, and chains were wound around the remaining parts as if to bind them. He had bat-like wings on his back. He realized that in the near future, his soul would depart from his body. Before that happened, he sought to gather prana at the Tree of Life and revive Atlantia as it once was, in order to prevent the extinction of the Shadow Angel tribe.",
        345: "Moroha was a war wing of the Shadow Angel tribe. He was a combat-type Shadow Angel with a appearance that fused human and insect, characterized by a pair of sword-shaped arms in addition to his normal arms, and insect-like wings on his back. The eyes visible through the cloth covering his face conveyed no emotion, giving him a strongly aggressive and intimidating presence. Belligerent and self-confident, he held a strong rivalry with Zushi and always took a challenging attitude toward him, but he possessed the ability to back it up. He owned his personal Cherudim soldier, the 'Cherudim Ischyron', which overwhelmed the Aquarion from start to finish.",
        346: 'Lenshi is the prototype wing of the Shadow Angels.\nBy adding mythic power to figures created with his own hands, he is able to forge Cherudim soldiers and Mythical Beasts. It is this very skill that earned him the reputation of having the fingertips of a god.\nHis dome-shaped body and mask, which appears to have lenses attached, give the impression of a scientist indulging in mad experiments within a laboratory. Two pairs of wings grow from the sides of his head.',
        347: 'Goushi is the wing of monstrous strength among the Shadow Angels.\nWith wings running from the crown of his head to his tail, he is a Shadow Angel of colossal frame, standing perhaps five meters tall. His disproportionately long and large arms evoke the ferocity of a wild beast.\nAmong the Shadow Angels, he is closest to Futaba, the small wing.',
        348: 'Futaba is the last small wing remaining among the Shadow Angels.\nShe has wings at her ankles, and parts of her body, such as her shoulders and arms, have machinery attached.\nAfter the Atlandia War twelve thousand years ago, children became almost nonexistent among the Shadow Angels, making her a precious presence, and she has been doted upon by the other Shadow Angels. Perhaps because of this, she has grown into a very spoiled and mischievous child.\nDriven by her naturally abundant curiosity, she constantly conceives and carries out pranks (though from a human perspective they are calamities akin to nightmares).',
        349: 'Shirua is the wing of information among the Shadow Angels.\nAs a wing governing wisdom and intelligence gathering, two beings of different colors together form a single entity. With wings on its back, the body of a lion, and a human face, it has the form of a sphinx.\nHe also serves as the caretaker of Futaba, the small wing, but his excessive fondness prevents him from taking a stern approach, which has only encouraged her willfulness.',
        350: 'Sirius defected to the Shadow Angels.\nBelieving without a doubt that he himself was the Wing of the Sun, he engaged Aquarion in fierce battle using the Cherudim Mars, a fusion of the Vector Mars and Cherudim soldiers.\nHowever, the truth he eventually heard from the lips of Zushi was something he had never even imagined.',
        351: "The strongest guardian Shadow Angel of the Shadow Angel tribe. Twelve thousand years ago, he unleashed his great power to hunt and slaughter countless humans. However, during battle he met the human female warrior Celiane, and the two fell in love with each other. Eventually he parted ways with the Shadow Angels and began fighting alongside humanity, using the 'Mechanical Angel Aquarion' to sink Atlandia into subspace. In the present day, Apollo carries his past life, and on rare occasions his personality surfaces.",
        352: "A brave human female warrior who fought the Shadow Angels twelve thousand years ago. She met Apollonius during battle, and despite being enemies, the two fell in love. Later they joined forces and defeated the Shadow Angels with the 'Mechanical Angel Aquarion.' In the present day, Silvia carries Celiane's past life, and on rare occasions her personality surfaces.",
        353: "A fourteen-year-old boy whose father was a hero who once saved the world. He has a straightforward personality - simple, pure-hearted, bright, and positive. Because of this, he has a tendency to lose sight of his surroundings when he gets too absorbed in something. Also, everything he thinks shows on his face, which makes him a target for teasing from the adults around him. He is also at that age where being seen through the lens of being a hero's son is a source of frustration. He lives alone with his grandfather in the rural town of Bellforest, and while dissatisfied with his boring, unchanging daily life, he spent his days aimlessly devoting himself to his bike and lift board. However, when he fell in love at first sight with Eureka, who suddenly descended from the sky, he became a member of Gekkostate at the invitation of his idol Holland and her. While being worked hard as an errand boy, he boarded the Nirvash alongside Eureka during sorties. At first he only sat in the sub-seat, but gradually he began to show promise as a rider. Eventually he came to hold an indispensable presence for Gekkostate and for Eureka.",
        354: 'In the final episode, Renton rose up to save Eureka. His slightly longer hair and resolute expression show considerable growth. And the Nirvash, responding to his feelings, evolved into Spec 3.',
        355: "An LFO rider belonging to Gekkostate who pilots the Nirvash. She is a girl with mysterious abilities, able to hear the voices of LFOs and machines to communicate with them, and read the flow of invisible Trapar currents. Her words and actions are far removed from common sense, her emotions are subdued, and she rarely shows a smile. However, drawn along by Renton's brightness, she gradually opened her heart. She serves as a surrogate mother to three orphaned children, and when she was first called 'Mom,' it astonished Renton.",
        356: "Eureka after being absorbed into the Scub and rescued. She is in fact a humanoid Coralian, and according to the high priest of the Vodarac, she was in a state called the 'Seventh Observation World' (humans exist in the Third Observation World). After waking up, she became aware of the feelings for Renton budding within her, and showed the decisiveness and initiative to go out alone to search for Renton, who had run away from home.",
        357: 'Eureka after meeting Sakuya and crossing the Zone together with Renton and the children. Having returned to the Third Observation World, her hair and blood vessels have reverted to their state before being absorbed into the Scub.',
        358: 'Eureka, whose body underwent changes as if triggered by the breakthrough of the Zone. Her left arm became a translucent green, and similar discoloration appeared in various parts of her body. On her back, organs resembling a combination of butterfly wings and the fins of marine creatures have grown.',
        359: 'The leader of the anti-establishment group Gekkostate. 29 years old. He possesses such lift technique that he became the youngest champion in the amateur lift world tournament, and is a charismatic figure among lift boarders. Renton also had a strong admiration for him, putting posters in his room and using a replica lift board. He is excessively confident and always leads the members with a strong attitude. Yet during lifts he never loses his composure, which is what makes him who he is. He once belonged to the Federation of the Tower State military, but defected after a certain incident. He seized the Gekko-Goh and the Nirvash and organized Gekkostate. He and Talho are lovers, but because all his actions prioritize Eureka above all, this has become a source of trouble. With Renton, who in some ways resembles his former self, it seems minor clashes are constant.',
        360: 'One of the LFO riders of the Gekko-Goh. 25 years old. He has a light, easygoing personality and is an avid music lover. He possesses such keen hearing that he can detect subtle noises that ordinary people cannot distinguish. He keeps a large record collection in his room. He is completely smitten with his girlfriend Hilda, and whenever he cracks a joke he gets scolded, leaving him utterly unable to talk back.',
        361: 'A female LFO rider aboard the Gekko-Goh. 25 years old.\nShe is close friends with Talho and serves as a good advisor to the often troubled woman. She is romantically involved with Matthew and bosses him around without restraint in daily life, maintaining deep ties with the other members as well.\nHaving once worked as a civil servant, she excels at handling matters briskly and efficiently. As a result, in the loose and male-dominated Gekkostate, without her efforts various affairs would fall into disorder.',
        362: "A cameraman accompanying the Gekkostate. 30 years old.\nHe fights with a pen mightier than the sword, handling the writing and editing for the magazine 'ray=out' published to spread word of the Gekkostate's activities to the world.\nWhen battle begins, he boards the rear seat of the R606 and devotes himself to taking photographs on the battlefield. At such times he gives Matthew detailed instructions on altitude and speed, and true to his words 'Art is something you put your life on the line for,' he shows a nerve steadier than any rider.",
        363: "The helmsman of the Gekko-Goh. 26 years old.\nShe is highly intelligent and beautiful, a talented woman who also graces the cover of 'ray=out' as a model. Yet beneath her appearance, she is strong-willed to the point of excess, and harsh words fly from her mouth the moment she speaks. Seeing Renton seems to stir her mischievous side, and she often bullies him.\nShe and Holland have been lovers since they deserted the military together. However, she did not take kindly to Holland's evasive attitude or his behavior of always centering everything on Eureka, and she made no effort to hide her aversion.",
        364: 'Inspired by the changing Eureka, and having conceived a child with Holland, Talho resolved to change herself. As a first step, she altered her hairstyle and clothing, giving a considerably calmer impression both inside and out.\nShe left all navigation of the Gekko-Goh to Moondoggie, and served as captain in place of Holland, who sortied in an LFO.',
        365: "The sub-leader of the Gekkostate. 29 years old.\nHe is a childhood friend of Holland and serves as a good advisor. There are also rumors that it was Hap who urged Holland to desert the military.\nHe has a gentle personality and never loses his smile, but he still retains a mischievous streak, such as taking the lead in teasing Renton. In battle, however, he shows a surprising calm.\nHe is also in charge of the Gekkostate's finances, taking on jobs and urging thrift, and his daily management is full of hardship. The members' wasteful spending, which never improves, weighs heavily on him.\nHe has a habit of stripping completely naked when answering the call of nature.",
        366: 'Gunner aboard the Gekko-Goh. 45 years old.\nAs his appearance and manner suggest, he was a strict military man, but his encounter with Holland shook his entire outlook on life, and from then on he began to act alongside the Gekko-Goh.\nHe is the oldest of the official Gekkostate members, and his presence - one could call it the presence of a leader - and deep combat experience make him a dependable man.\nHis skill with firearms is considerable, from hitting enemy ships with laser cannons from beyond their range to using the recoil of the main cannon for emergency evasive maneuvers.',
        367: "A member of Gekkostate. 16 years old.\nHe has a beautiful appearance, but when he opens his mouth he speaks with a heavy accent. He himself is self-conscious about this gap, and so he speaks little.\nHe was the comedy relief among the members, but when the newcomer Renton threatened his position, he briefly harbored a rivalry. Yet after various twists and turns, Renton came to call him 'Brother Doggy' and look up to him. Perhaps due to a certain kinship, the two seem to get along quite well.\nHe is secretly troubled by having no role during combat, and at times one could see him taking it out on his partner Gidget and on the children.",
        368: "Communications officer aboard the Gekko-Goh. 15 years old.\nSomewhat prone to cleanliness obsession and a bit of a fan girl, she is nevertheless one of the Gekko-Goh's idols alongside the small, bright-natured Eureka.\nShe has feelings for Moondoggie, and whenever not in combat she is always clinging to him and fussing over him.",
        369: "A genius mechanic on the Gekko-Goh, in charge of hardware. 33 years old.\nHe joined Gekkostate after reading 'ray=out,' feeling a kinship with it, and boarding the Gekko-Goh on his own initiative.\nWith his cleanly shaved head, refined features, and neat attire, he is a nervous perfectionist and thorough realist, and he is best friends with Woz, who is the complete opposite in all of these ways.",
        370: "A genius mechanic on the Gekko-Goh, in charge of software. 33 years old.\nHe joined Gekkostate after reading 'ray=out,' feeling a kinship with it, and boarding the Gekko-Goh on his own initiative.\nHe is an easygoing and strong dreamer, reflected in his unkempt long hair, plain appearance, and rough, flashy clothing. He is best friends with Jobs, who is the complete opposite in all of these ways.",
        371: 'Misha is the resident doctor of the Gekko-Goh. She is 40 years old. Since her time serving in the Federation military, she was devoted to researching Eureka, and her reason for leaving the military was to continue examining Eureka. Always calm and possessed of rich life experience, she often plays the role of a counselor as well as a doctor. However, she herself denies this.',
        372: "Gonji is an old man living on the Gekko-Goh whose purpose, identity, and age are all unknown, a man of many mysteries. Appearing and disappearing at will, he shows up all over the ship and asks, 'Would you like some tea?' His fortune-telling boasts a considerable accuracy rate, and he is regarded with respect by the members of Gekkostate.",
        373: "Maeter is one of the three orphans on the Gekko-Goh. She is 4 years old. She has a strong competitive spirit and a precocious personality. She calls Eureka 'Mama' and adores her, and was hostile toward Renton, who appeared suddenly and approached Eureka. However, her wariness softened in the face of Renton's earnestness, and eventually she warmed up to him.",
        374: "Link is one of the three orphans on the Gekko-Goh. He is 3 years old. Being the youngest, he is quite clingy. He calls Eureka 'Mama' and adores her, and was hostile toward Renton, who appeared suddenly and approached Eureka. However, his wariness softened in the face of Renton's earnestness, and eventually he warmed up to him.",
        375: "Maurice is one of the three orphans on the Gekko-Goh. He is 5 years old. He speaks little and is very shy around strangers, but at times shows the initiative and independence befitting the oldest of the group. He calls Eureka 'Mama' and adores her, and was hostile toward Renton, who appeared suddenly and approached Eureka. However, his wariness softened in the face of Renton's earnestness, and eventually he warmed up to him.",
        376: "Renton's grandfather. A stubborn old man with a craftsman's temperament that shows on his face. He is a person of deep human feeling, genuinely worrying about his grandson, angered at the military for concealing the fact of his son's death, and showing kindness to small children. He is apparently well known among diggers, and in that circle he is more famous than the hero Adroc. He demonstrates the peculiar technique inherited by his grandson of 'tuning machines to be peaky,' and the motorcycle he repaired for Dominic left the latter sighing in exasperation.",
        377: "Renton's father. Deceased. A hero said to have saved humanity from the great disaster 'Summer of Love' caused by the abnormal Trapar phenomenon that struck the world, and he is said to have died at the same time. His date of death is September 10, 11990. He is widely known and popular worldwide. He appears in history textbooks, a beer bearing his name has been released, and in Renton's hometown of Contrado there is even a song praising him.",
        378: "Renton's older sister. She disappeared several years ago and has been missing ever since. In the story, Renton's monologue of 'Nee-san...' is inserted at every turn. Since she served as a mother substitute for him, it seems he has not been able to become independent from her.",
        379: 'A captain who leads the Izumo squad in the Federation military of the Tower State. Stubborn and foul-mouthed, but a born soldier who applies himself earnestly to his duties. He did not look favorably upon Dominic, who came aboard as an observer. He frequently encountered the Gekko-Goh during the capture of the Nirvash TypeZERO and during Coralian investigations, engaging in fierce battles.',
        380: "A soldier belonging to the Intelligence Section 7 of the Tower State Federation military. His rank is lieutenant. 20 years old. A basically capable young man who attained the rank of lieutenant at a young age. However, contrary to his appearance, he is stubborn and quick-tempered, severely directionally challenged and unable to read maps, and vomits at the sight of corpses - he has many flaws that hardly befit a soldier. He serves as Anemone's caretaker, managing her with orders and medication, while secretly harboring romantic feelings for her. He had long been devoted to Dewey and assisted him as a trusted subordinate. Even during Dewey's imprisonment, he continued contact without minding being relegated to a menial post, and eventually returned to the military mainstream alongside Dewey.",
        381: "Dewey Novak was a military officer belonging to the intelligence division of the Tower State Federation military. His rank was lieutenant colonel, aged 36. At first glance, he had a calm and quiet appearance, but the coldness and ambition hidden beneath were immeasurable. He had been confined for a long time in the form of taking responsibility for a certain incident, but when the Seven Swell phenomenon occurred, he was released by the three sages and promoted to colonel at the same time. He took command of the entire military and began to act in order to carry out the 'Ageha Plan' proposed by Adroc.",
        382: 'Anemone was a girl belonging to the Tower State Federation military who piloted the Nirvash type the END. She kept a mysterious creature called Gulliver, whose thoughts were impossible to discern, as a pet. Her emotions fluctuated violently, and she was extremely selfish and capricious in nature. She constantly gave trouble to Dominic, who served as her caretaker, but she showed a straightforwardness fitting for a girl of her age in front of Dewey. While suppressing the unbearable headaches that frequently came upon her with medication, she repeatedly fought against Eureka and Renton.',
        383: 'Charles Beams was a transporter who, along with his beloved wife Ray, flew around the world in the Swan. He was a generous and manly man of good cheer. He happened to meet Renton, who had run away from home, hit it off with him, and treated him like his own son. There was even a time when he tried to make Renton his adopted son, but the situation changed completely due to a casual remark Renton made.',
        384: 'Ray Beams was a transporter who, along with her beloved husband Charles, flew around the world in the Swan. She was a deeply emotional woman, and her cooking skills were a source of pride for Charles. She affectionately cared for Renton, who she happened to meet while he had run away from home, like her own son. Ray, whose body could not bear children, at one time considered making Renton her adopted son. But the situation changed completely due to a casual remark Renton made.',
        385: "Greg Bear Eagan was a leading authority in Archetype research who advocated the theory that Scub Coral was intelligent. Despite his huge build and mohawk, he had a gentle personality contrary to his name, and sweets were his favorite. He was called by the nickname 'Doctor Bear'.",
        386: 'The director of the Trezor Technical Research Institute, a research facility directly under the command of the Atlantic Federation military. Despite holding a military position, he has a fateful personality in that when he encounters an interesting research subject, he cannot suppress his impulses as a researcher.',
        387: 'A believer of Vodarak. A wanted person pursued by the Atlantic Federation military, he was protected by Gekkostate and headed for the holy land.',
        388: 'A high priest of Vodarak. He is the man who once taught Holland the truth of this world and gave the impetus for the founding of Gekkostate. However, he was a corrupt priest whose bizarre behavior was conspicuous - he hated baths, loved mayonnaise dearly, and suddenly had the members of Gekkostate play soccer. A Compac Drive was embedded in his chest, granting him mysterious powers.',
        389: 'A humanoid Coralian discovered before Eureka, worshipped as a saint by Vodarak believers. She fell in love with Norbu, who was once her caretaker, and together they attempted to enter the Zone, but failed and she became Compac. For the following forty years, she protected the Vodarak Palace with a barrier.',
        390: "A scientist belonging to Trezor Technical Research Institute, serving as head of the Technology Development Division. Normally serious and calm, she quickly becomes hysterical when something intolerable appears before her. Gekkostate's reckless behavior seemed to be too much for her, and she frequently lost her temper. She is an old acquaintance of Misha. At the time Eureka was discovered, she was involved in her investigation and research.",
        391: "Anemone's pet.\nIt uses its special ability (?) of increasing its body weight and crushing down on those it dislikes. The victim of this was almost always Dominic.\nSince its expression never changes, it is impossible to tell what it is thinking.",
        392: "A member of the 'Ageha Squad' organized by Dewey to carry out the Ageha Project.\nThe Ageha Squad was composed only of extremely capable and beautiful boys.",
        393: "A member of the 'Ageha Squad' organized by Dewey to carry out the Ageha Project.\nEvery member of the Ageha Squad possessed a cold-heartedness that paid no heed to the deaths of unspecified numbers of people, and acted only for Dewey's sake.",
        394: "One of the three sages who made up the 'Council of Sages,' the de facto rulers of the Pledgio Tower State Federation.\nHe also held strong influence over the Tower State Federation military.",
        395: "One of the three sages who made up the 'Council of Sages,' the de facto rulers of the Pledgio Tower State Federation.\nHe also held strong influence over the Tower State Federation military.",
        396: "Braya is one of the three sages comprising the 'Council of Sages,' which serves as the de facto ruler of the PLoS Federation. He holds significant influence over the PLoS Federation military as well.",
        397: "Setsuko Ohara is a pilot belonging to the Earth Federation military's technical research unit 'Glory Star'. She holds the rank of second lieutenant and is 19 years old. She has a serious, earnest personality and strives diligently to fulfill the tasks and roles assigned to her. However, due to her lack of self-confidence and timid nature, she tends to be passive in her approach to things, and inwardly she harbors doubts about whether a soldier's life truly suits her. Although she has no combat experience, her careful piloting skill is highly regarded, and she has been newly assigned to Glory Star. Her hobby is going around tasting sweets at various shops.",
        398: "Denzel Hammer is a pilot belonging to 'Glory Star' and serves as the team captain. He holds the rank of captain and is 34 years old. A veteran with abundant combat experience, his record earned him the appointment as captain of Glory Star, which conducts evaluation tests of new machines. Despite his intimidating appearance, he is attentive to detail and takes good care of his subordinates. He is naturally an easygoing person, but he is conscious of his age and responsibility, and strives to make sound judgments in any situation. His favorite thing is cold beer.",
        399: "Toby Watson is a pilot belonging to 'Glory Star' and serves as the team's sub-chief. He holds the rank of first lieutenant and is 22 years old. He was an ace pilot in another unit, and his skill earned him a transfer to Glory Star when it was founded. He is cheerful and talkative, serving as the team's mood maker, yet on the battlefield he cuts into the enemy formation first and with cold judgment steadily drives enemy machines into a corner. He has many hobbies and shows interest in everything. He also has a fiancee back in his hometown.",
        400: "Rand Travis is a man who runs the wandering repair shop 'Beater Service'. He is 27 years old. He calls himself 'The Heat,' a bold and unrestrained hot-blooded man. However, when his blood boils he often goes too far, and behind his back he is called 'The Crusher.' He greatly dislikes that nickname, and his mood rapidly sours when he hears it. He regards a drink after work as his supreme pleasure, and for that he pilots Gunleon and devotes himself to his repair shop business. He travels the desolate land with Mel in search of his missing master.",
        401: "Mel Beater is the daughter of Ciero Beater, Rand's master. Despite her childlike appearance, she is actually 16 years old. She has a spirited and playful personality, and her hobby is writing a diary. She has known Rand since he first became Ciero's apprentice, and she claims to be his fiancee. At Beater Service, she handles sales and accounting, and also serves as the sub-pilot for Gunleon.",
        402: "Ciero Beater is Mel's father and Rand's master in repair work. He took in Rand, a former thug, to work and live with him, literally instilling the spirit of a smile into him through rigorous training. He was a highly skilled and popular repairman, but four years ago he was caught up in a space-time displacement and his whereabouts became unknown.",
        403: "Eder Bernal is a major general in the New Earth Federation Forces. She is a powerful figure within the military who was promoted to major general in recognition of her achievements in establishing the UN. She has a gentle and thoughtful personality, worries about the future of the multi-dimensional world, and has many followers within the military. She intends to reform the corrupt upper echelons from within, and to that end she directs her personal special operations unit, Kaimera, to secretly support various organizations and individuals. She carries herself with refined manners and never loses her Madonna-like smile, but she will occasionally resort to physical force to stop Dr. Z's rampages.",
        404: "Eder Bernal is a major general in the New Earth Federation Forces. She has begun taking action to bring the entire world under her control, aiming to become the 'Ruler of the New World'.",
        405: "Dr. Z is the true identity of Eder Bernal, and the man who created the android Eder Bernal. He has succeeded in limited control of the power of the Origin Law, and he uses that power to act on his own desires. His principle of action is summed up in the phrase 'As long as it's interesting!' and he enjoys the existence of the multi-dimensional world born from the space-time vibration bomb more than anyone else. By applying the power of the Origin Law, he integrates the abilities of multiple selves existing between parallel worlds, surpassing ordinary humans in every respect. Furthermore, he is liberated from concepts such as ethics and morality, and is driven by desires that others find difficult to understand, making his intentions and actions hard to predict.",
        406: 'An elderly scientist who serves Edel Bernal. His specialties are mechanical engineering and time-space control technology, and he develops mobile weapons for the Chimera. He always overwhelms those around him with his high energy, and he is very fond of Brigadier General Edel.',
        407: 'A soldier of the New Earth Federation military. He is the captain of Chimera First Squad, with the rank of lieutenant. He fights to reform the New Earth Federation military and to establish order across the multi-dimensional world. He is a serious, honest, and pure young man, but he has a tendency to be afraid of women. He and Lieutenant Shuran of Chimera Second Squad are close friends.',
        408: "A soldier of the New Earth Federation military. He is the captain of Chimera Second Squad under Edel's direct command, with the rank of lieutenant. He shows his true worth in rear-area missions such as maintaining public order and information warfare. Because he is calm and composed and never loses his cool demeanor no matter the situation, he sometimes gives others a cold impression. He and Raven are close friends.",
        409: 'A mysterious woman who cooperates with Asakim. She pilots the mobile weapon Eliphas and appears in various situations. She always wears a bewitching smile, but she has a fierce and radical personality and shows no mercy to those who oppose her.',
        410: 'A young man in black robes, shrouded entirely in mystery. His purpose is unknown, but he acts under an unwavering conviction. He pilots the jet-black humanoid mobile weapon Shurouga, appearing like a swift wind.',
    },
}
